        </h3>

        <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: #374151; margin: 0 0 14px 0; line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
            The <strong>Web-Based AI-Assisted Individualized Education Plan Management and Generation System</strong> provides school personnel with a centralized workspace to manage student profiles, structure daily classroom observations, formulate measurable learning goals, and streamline periodic reporting. By accessing and operating the system, you agree to the following Terms and Conditions:
        </p>

        <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: disc; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #374151; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
            <li style="line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
                <strong>User Accountability and Role-Based Access:</strong> School personnel (Administrators and SPED Teachers) are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of their login credentials and for all actions performed under their accounts. System access is strictly governed by Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Personnel must operate exclusively within their assigned access levels and are strictly prohibited from attempting to bypass system restrictions, view unauthorized student data, or alter account permissions beyond their designated responsibilities.
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
                <strong>Data Privacy Act Compliance (R.A. 10173):</strong> School users handle highly sensitive student information, including diagnostic profiles (e.g., Autism Spectrum Disorder, ADHD), and baseline evaluations. Personnel agree to comply strictly with the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012, ensuring student files and encrypted database records remain confidential and accessed solely on a legitimate, need-to-know pedagogical basis.
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
                <strong>Mandatory Human-in-the-Loop Validation:</strong> All artificial intelligence integrations—including the AI Daily Log Standardizer, SMART Goal Generator, AI Progress Summarizer, and Home Recommendation Assistant—serve strictly as drafting aids. SPED Teachers and Administrators agree that all AI outputs must undergo human verification, pedagogical review, and manual editing prior to publishing daily reports or periodic summaries. Personnel remain fully accountable for the educational appropriateness and accuracy of finalized records.
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
                <strong>Report Approval and Digital Stamp Authorization:</strong> The partner institution complies with the adoption of an authorized digital stamp to authenticate school records generated by the system. School Administrators must formally review and approve all periodic summaries before they are published to the guardian portal. Approving a document automatically appends the Administrator’s digital stamp and signature, confirming the report's official status.
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
                <strong>Scope and Functional Boundaries:</strong> Personnel acknowledge that the system is strictly limited to IEP-related behavioral, academic, and developmental documentation. It must not be utilized for standardized diagnostic clinical scoring, external medical monitoring, tuition/billing, or general school admissions outside the defined scope of Dreams Achievers Learning Center PH.
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify;">
                <strong>Record Retention, Archiving, and Account Termination:</strong> Administrators agree to follow standardized archiving protocols, including executing Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) prior to initiating Year-End Rollovers and capturing student snapshots. Dreams Achievers Learning Center PH reserves the right to suspend or revoke system access for any user who violates data handling policies, misuses AI generation utilities, or breaches student record confidentiality.
            </li>
